  Illustration: {fileID: 21300000, guid: 81fb0905a4c5b214e832e47d7a64203a, type: 3}
  OverviewText: Sea lampreys spread into the Great Lakes through canals built by
    people. They fed on fish that were not adapted to defend themselves. Their population
    grew larger than the ecosystem could balance. As ecological disruptors, they
    changed food webs and harmed many fish species.
